-- title:
--   Shifted Lévy running-supremum dividend measure has no nonpositive-time mass
-- statement:
--   For any sample path of a spectrally negative Lévy process and any finite time shift u, the Stieltjes dividend measure generated by the running supremum of future Lévy increments has zero mass on (-∞,0]. The shifted path is bounded above on each compact interval, so its running supremum is monotone; its right-continuity follows from the proven shifted-supremum continuity lemma. The generic right-limit Stieltjes support theorem finishes the proof. This exactly supplies the missing hνneg hypothesis in the post-upcrossing dividend-measure map theorem and the discounted post-upcrossing translation, without treating the shifted path as a new Lévy object.
-- source:
--   Proved levyPath_bddAbove_Icc, intervalSup_monotone_of_bddAbove, shiftedSup_right_continuous_of_levy, rightLim_comp_toNNReal_of_rightContinuous, dividendMeasure_Iic_zero_of_monotone_rightLim. Source-faithful bridge for Avram dividend Proposition 1 strong-Markov split.

